abels\n      id: check_labels\n      run: |\n        BLOCKING_LABELS=(\"do NOT merge yet\" \"s: on hold\")\n        PR_LABELS=$(jq -r '.pull_request.labels[].name' \"$GITHUB_EVENT_PATH\")\n        \n        for LABEL in \"${BLOCKING_LABELS[@]}\"; do\n          if [[ \"$PR_LABELS\" == *\"$LABEL\"* ]]; then\n            echo \"This PR has a blocking label: $LABEL\"\n            exit 1\n          fi\n        done\n        \n        echo \"No blocking labels found\"\n      env:\n        GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n\n    - name: Unblock Merge\n      if: ${{ steps.check_labels.outcome == 'success' }}\n      run: |\n        echo \"The PR does not have any blocking labels. Merging is allowed.\"\n\n```\n\nThis workflow is triggered whenever a pull request is labeled or unlabeled. It checks if the labels include any of the specified blocking labels. If any of the blocking labels are found, the workflow will exit with a non-zero status code, preventing the PR from being merged. If no blocking labels are found, the workflow allows the PR to be merged.\n\nMake sure to save this YAML file in the `.github/workflows` directory in your repository. When you create a pull request with the \"do NOT merge yet\" or \"s: on hold\" label, the workflow will block the PR from being merged.","turn_id":"turn_000003"},"target_developer_prompt":{"create_time":1695033154.847554,"event_index":2,"role":"user","source_node_id":"aaa23d6a-0d1e-4385-8350-be677a5fbc91","source_parent_id":"60a3f091-6812-4569-a3e5-0b71dc089599","source_record_index":2,"text":"Write a GitHub Action yml file that blocks the PR from merging when there is a label named \"do NOT merge yet\" or \"s: on hold\"","turn_id":"turn_000002"}},"csv_extraction":{"context":[{"category":"context","evidence_spans":["Write a GitHub Action yml file that blocks the PR from merging"],"item_id":"context_1","normalized_text":"The requested artifact is a GitHub Actions YAML file for a pull-request workflow.","source_roles":["user"]